pve-bcachefs (0.0.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Check that a derived project id is actually free before claiming it, against
    both the ids recorded on our own anchors and the filesystem's own quota
    state. The derivation is a bijection within one scheme but not across a
    change to one - an id assigned under the previous, narrower scheme could
    collide with one this scheme derives for a different guest - and the storage
    does not own the filesystem, so project quotas may be in use for something
    entirely outside PVE.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:15:00 +0200

pve-bcachefs (0.0.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Project ids now reserve 8 bits for the disk index rather than 4, so the low
    byte carries the index and the rest the vmid. 256 slots covers PVE's
    mp0..mp255 exactly; the previous 16 was arbitrary and would have refused a
    guest with more than sixteen volumes on one storage.
  * Existing volumes are unaffected: the id is recorded in trusted.pve.projid
    and read back from there, so only newly allocated volumes use the wider
    scheme and the two coexist.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0200

pve-bcachefs (0.0.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Snapshot mounting for path-backed subvolumes moved out to the new
    pve-lxc-snapshot-mount package and is now depended on rather than
    duplicated. It was never bcachefs-specific - it repairs the same gap for
    btrfs, an officially supported storage type - and carrying a copy here
    meant two packages racing to patch one file, held apart only by a comment
    string that happened to match.
  * Drop APPLY_LXC_PATCH. A storage plugin that only half works is not a
    configuration anyone wants, and the raw-image fallback already covers the
    case where the patch cannot be applied.
  * The patch script gains --revert, so removing the package reverses just its
    own change instead of restoring the whole file over another package's.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:45:00 +0200

pve-bcachefs (0.0.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * No changes to the plugin, the patch or the packaging: this release exists
    to exercise the release pipeline end to end - build, release, dispatch to
    the apt repository, and retention of earlier versions in the pool.
  * Releases now trigger apt repository publishing immediately, via the
    workflow dispatch endpoint rather than repository_dispatch, so the token
    involved needs only the Actions permission and not push access to code.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:45:00 +0200

pve-bcachefs (0.0.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaged release.
  * bcachefs storage plugin with subvolume container rootfs, native snapshots,
    clones and rollback, and per-storage bcachefs IO options.
  * Container size enforcement via bcachefs project quotas, with a raw-image
    fallback where the filesystem has no project quotas.
  * Patches PVE::LXC for sized subvolume rootfs volumes and snapshot-mode
    vzdump, re-applied automatically after pve-container upgrades.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
